The two native layers share 1,303,296 trained adapter parameters. The optimizer completed 720 AdamW updates over 109,336 output-token targets. Of those, 78,375 supervised opening lookups, 7,250 supervised post-observation conclusions, 7,150 supervised inline judgments and 16,561 came from WikiSQL rehearsal. The two short judgment types accounted for 13.2% of output-token exposure. The paired margin gave their first divergent label additional weight. Target counts alone do not measure gradient contribution. Each six-example batch contained two opposite-source pairs and two other turns. The loss combines ordinary response-token cross entropy with two context-specific logit margins on the first differing response token. Preparing frozen prefix states took 220.39 s and native optimization took 566.01 s. The original six-at-once run used 6.545 GiB, crossed its 6.50 GiB ceiling and ended before evaluating either model. This fit used physical groups of two, two, one and one with one optimizer update per logical batch. On the first sampled batch the MLX gradients differed by 0.01162 in relative L2 norm and the losses by 0.00017. The registered limits were 0.08 and 0.06, respectively.
